Minimum protected-intent relaxation is NP-hard.
A computed minimum relaxation is a proposal, not an authorization.
Vector-valued architectural consequences require a Pareto relaxation frontier.
Waivers
An authorized waiver creates a new intent theory.
A waiver does not retroactively prove old intent was preserved.
Intent versions preserve the historical distinction.
Sequence and relational intent
Architectural sequence can be represented as finite path-language constraints.
Relational intent can depend on several design objects jointly.
Independent coordinate bounds do not replace relational semantics.
Symmetry
A transformation invariant under the complete protected endpoint observation preserves endpoint intent.
Trace, authority, and authorship still require separate checking.
Preference refinement
Human judgment narrows the admitted preference family.
Preference inconsistency is surfaced rather than converted into a fake average.
