74. What Has Now Been Proven
Semantic versus concrete states
Semantic design states, partial concrete states, concrete artifacts, serialized packages, and physical buildings are distinct mathematical levels.
Exact materialization is a relation between a semantic specification and a concrete artifact.
The materialization fiber contains every concrete artifact realizing one semantic specification.
Realizability means nonemptiness of that exact fiber.
UNRESOLVED is distinct from proven emptiness.
Materialization fibers
Canonical quotient classes are inhabited by definition.
Recombined abstract descriptors may lie outside the image of the concrete abstraction map.
A semantic state may have no, one, many, or infinitely many concrete witnesses.
The source kind of a semantic state must remain explicit.
Constructive witnesses
A checked materialization result is a dependent pair containing both the artifact and its proof.
A bare existential proposition is not automatically an executable CAD or BIM artifact.
Finite exact extension queries can construct a witness coordinate by coordinate.
Exact separator-DP backpointers reconstruct global witnesses.
Existence versus extraction
Finite surjective abstraction maps admit set-theoretic sections.
Section existence does not prove efficient computability.
Heuristic search failure does not prove unrealizability.
Restricted finite realizability is NP-complete.
Symmetry and noncanonical witnesses
A symmetry-invariant semantic state may have no equivariant deterministic materializer when its fiber has no group-fixed witness.
Selecting one symmetric witness can require an explicit tie breaker, objective, or human choice.
Claim transport
Fiber-invariant claims factor through the semantic state.
Certified fiber-invariant claims transport to every concrete witness.
Claims varying inside one fiber cannot be determined from the semantic state alone.
Proof transport must therefore be explicit and claim specific.
Materialization theory and width
Materialization contextual equivalence is Prompt-2 equivalence under an expanded experiment theory.
A richer materialization theory refines decision equivalence.
Materialization width can exceed decision width.
A decision-sufficient interface may be too coarse for concrete gluing.
Realization-complete interfaces
Exact local substitution requires every cross-boundary materialization dependency to factor through the interface.
Omitted connector, access, resource, tolerance, or evidence dependencies make substitution unsound.
Refinement towers
Compatible refinement maps compose.
Finite surjective refinement stages admit end-to-end lifts.
Independent nonempty adjacent refinement relations do not guarantee one compatible chain.
Local-to-global gluing
Running intersection plus exact separator agreement yields globally consistent variable assignments.
Compatible local witnesses glue over a realization-complete join tree.
Pairwise consistency is insufficient on cyclic covers.
Fully semijoin-consistent acyclic relations admit global extensions.
Separator-DP reconstruction
A separator DP is constructive only when it retains witnesses, backpointers, or an exact extraction oracle.
Accepted root messages reconstruct a complete global witness under the gluing hypotheses.
Geometric and topological realization
Exact topology and quantitative geometry are distinct.
Numerical geometry error, construction tolerance, and physical discrepancy are distinct.
Mandatory geometric predicates whose enclosures cross a boundary remain unresolved.
Abstract topology requires a checked geometric embedding.
Entity lineage
Semantic entities may split or merge into concrete entity families.
Claims, products, consent, and authorship scopes must be transported through explicit lineage.
Product instantiation
Abstract roles require exact product or fabrication identities.
Complete materialization contextual equivalence justifies product substitution.
Equal capacity alone does not justify substitution.
Product-family optimization is NP-hard in a restricted subclass.
Catalog and discretization gaps
Continuous semantic optima may be unattainable under discrete catalogs.
Such optima remain valid lower bounds when correctly derived.
Catalog gaps contribute to the materialization gap.
Tolerance robustness
Tolerance is represented as a joint relation rather than independent intervals by default.
Nominal, fixed robust, adjustable robust, and scenario-specific realizability are different propositions.
Scenario-specific designs do not constitute one precommitted robust artifact.
Adjustable recourse can be strictly stronger than fixed robustness.
Shared tolerance variables must preserve correlation.
Adjustable and nonanticipative realization
A recourse policy may depend only on information available when the action is chosen.
Clairvoyant scenario plans need not yield a nonanticipative policy.
Relative-displacement bounds certify robust clearance under explicit sign and correlation assumptions.
Static versus sequential constructibility
A clash-free final artifact need not be constructible.
A checked legal sequence is an existential constructibility witness under the declared action theory.
Temporary-state safety is a first-class requirement.
BIM and document coherence
Documents are scoped projections of an authoritative artifact.
Single-source projections agree on shared authoritative data.
Manual edits or stale versions violate projection coherence unless reconciled.
Display rounding is not authoritative compliance data.
Serialization fidelity
Round-trip serialization preserves only the declared export experiment theory.
Geometry-only export does not prove preservation of evidence, products, consent, or sequence semantics.
Materialization gaps
The materialization gap measures the difference between a valid semantic lower bound and the concrete optimum.
The gap can be strictly positive.
A concrete incumbent and valid global lower bound certify concrete (\varepsilon)-optimality.
Materialization CEGAR
Checked witnesses are real.
Cuts proved to exclude only empty fibers preserve every concrete possibility.
UNKNOWN cannot justify a witness or cut.
Finite exact feasibility CEGAR terminates under strict progress and fair terminating oracles.
Human-option preservation
A materialization fiber may contain architecturally distinct witnesses.
Arbitrary selection from such a fiber can destroy a legitimate human option.
ANANKE must refine the state, preserve several witnesses, or obtain an authorized choice.
Incremental rematerialization
Complete dependency graphs permit exact localized invalidation.
Under the stated hypotheses, incremental rematerialization checking agrees with cold checking.
Unchanged realization-complete interfaces form valid propagation frontiers.
Adversarial materialization testing
Product, tolerance, gluing, sequence, document, proof-transport, and sovereignty claims can be attacked through Prompt-10 Claim Breakers.
A found breaker invalidates only the scoped materialization claim it actually breaks.
Prompt-9 scheduling integration
Witness extraction, geometric refinement, tolerance certification, product instantiation, and construction sequencing become ordinary Prompt-9 computation actions.
Prompt 13 does not create a competing scheduler.
Prompt-11 release integration
A PCMP is an evidence artifact, not the whole release case.
Prompt-11 release remains blocked if a required materialization obligation is unresolved.
An independent checker can verify a PCMP without trusting the optimizer’s search history.
Prompt-12 sovereignty integration
The materializer must preserve active hard intent, authority, consent, provenance, and human options.
Materialization does not acquire the right to choose among architecturally distinct witnesses merely because their engineering reports match.
Whole-project proof-carrying materialization
Under the complete stated hypotheses, an accepted concrete artifact lies in the exact materialization fiber of the selected semantic specification.
Every transported or rechecked claim in the accepted proof ledger holds under its declared scope.
With a certified (U-L\le\varepsilon) gap, the artifact is concretely (\varepsilon)-optimal over the admitted concrete universe.
The central result is:
[ \boxed{ \begin{minipage}{0.89\linewidth} ANANKE can move from compressed semantic state to exact build artifact without losing correctness only by making materialization itself a typed, constructive, proof-carrying computation. \end{minipage} } ]



