49. Physical Reconciliation Frontiers
DEF-PHY32 — Physical Reconciliation Frontier
A node (q) is a Physical Reconciliation Frontier for changed root set (R) when:
every path from (R) to relevant downstream release roots passes through (q);
the complete downstream-visible report at (q) is unchanged;
its evidence, scope, and version remain applicable;
downstream rules inspect the upstream region only through that report.



THM-PHY24 — An Unchanged Physical Reconciliation Frontier Stops Downstream Semantic Recertification
Under DEF-PHY32’s conditions, no downstream semantic report changes because of the upstream field change.
