The execution law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{A legal construction sequence proves that the building can be built that way. It does not prove that it was built that way.} } ]
The evidence law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{Field records become physical knowledge only through explicit, applicable, checked relations between evidence and physical state.} } ]
The estimation law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{Do not collapse physical uncertainty to a point merely because software prefers one model. Preserve every physical world the evidence has not eliminated.} } ]
The calibration law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{An authentic measurement without valid calibration is authentic data, not automatically valid physical evidence.} } ]
The conformance law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{Certify conformance when every physical state consistent with the evidence conforms. Certify nonconformance when none can conform. Otherwise remain unresolved.} } ]
The identifiability law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{Do not measure hidden physical distinctions merely to know them. Measure them when they can still change a required claim.} } ]
The topology law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{A topology change is not a small coordinate error merely because its displacement is small.} } ]
The recourse law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{A repair is pre-certified only when the observed deviation, available information, allowed action, and resulting physical state all lie inside the approved recourse contract.} } ]
The nonanticipativity law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{A family of repairs chosen with knowledge of the future is not one executable field policy.} } ]
The temporary-state law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{A safe finished building does not excuse an unsafe construction state.} } ]
The commissioning law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{A commissioning test proves what its tested state and valid generalization theorem support—no more.} } ]
The release law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{Physical release does not require knowing the exact building microstate. It requires every physical state still compatible with trusted evidence to satisfy every required release claim.} } ]
The open-world law is:
[ \boxed{ \textbf{No field-evidence system proves the absence of physical deviations that its action, measurement, and threat theory never admitted.} } ]
The deepest Prompt-14 principle is:
[ \boxed{ \begin{minipage}{0.91\linewidth} ANANKE crosses the gap from design to reality only when construction actions, measurements, deviations, field repairs, scans, inspections, and commissioning results are treated as proof-carrying evidence about a physical state that may remain partially unknown. The objective is not to pretend the digital model is the building. The objective is to prove that every physical building still compatible with what has actually been observed is good enough for the claims we are prepared to make. \end{minipage} } ]
