48. Open-World Reliability Limitation
THM-REL34 — No Closed Reliability Theory Proves Absence of an Unmodeled Failure Mechanism
There exist two target worlds that:
agree on every state variable, failure mode, observation, and model in the current reliability theory;
differ by one unmodeled latent failure mechanism;
have different future mission outcomes.
Proof
Augment physical reality with hidden bit
[ q\in{0,1} ]
that is absent from every modeled state and observation.
Let all represented variables evolve identically in both worlds.
When (q=0), no additional failure occurs.
When (q=1), a hidden transition causes failure during the mission.
Every reliability artifact inside the closed theory is identical.
The actual mission outcome differs.
Therefore the closed theory cannot prove absence of the omitted mechanism. ∎
Reliability assurance is theory scoped.



