Option expiry: verify minimum of expiry and lead-time date.
Viability recursion: compare with exhaustive robust policies.
Frontier urgency: wait action leaves viability kernel.
Commitment closure: exact closure gives zero pure information value.
Option-enabling hardness: recover a known Weighted Set Cover optimum.
Scenario-tree growth: verify (2^k) terminal histories.
Architectural sovereignty: valuable option lacks authority and is rejected.
Prompt-13 materialization: semantic option without enabling geometry is rejected.
Prompt-18 execution: physically live but economically dead option.
Prompt-17 probability: probabilistic exercise not labeled robust.
Prompt-16 fleet update: transfer changes value but not current physical liveness.
Prompt-9 separation: computation changes knowledge; commitment changes continuation fiber.
Prompt-10 option breaker: hidden supplier common cause invalidates option.
Incremental/cold: exact agreement after one changed commitment root.
Malicious AI policy: invalid clairvoyant policy rejected.
