66. What Has Now Been Proven
Commitment semantics
The continuation fiber is the set of admissible nonanticipative future policies.
Conditioning on a current action restricts the continuation fiber.
A strict semantic commitment removes at least one decision-relevant future report.
Commitment is relative to the future experiment and report theory.
The commitment relation is a preorder over aligned nodes.
Reversibility
Exact recovery implies contextual reversibility.
Contextual reversibility composes when the recovery words respect contextual congruence.
Physical reversibility does not imply economic, contractual, evidentiary, or sovereignty reversibility.
A reversibility claim must specify its dimension and bound.
Equal final geometry does not establish equal project state.
Causal flexibility
Present observational equivalence does not imply equal future action affordances.
Option-aware equivalence must include future action experiments.
Restricting the action theory can merge causal states.
Causal width cannot increase when future actions are removed.
A future thaw may require state discarded during freeze.
Options
A real engineering option requires an exercise action, window, preconditions, rights, authority, evidence, and execution path.
A valid enabling witness establishes exercise only inside its certified domain.
A conceptual redesign is not automatically an option.
Geometric modularity alone does not prove flexibility.
A live-option set and its decision-relevant opportunity image are different objects.
Option count does not determine option value.
Value
There is no unique model-independent scalar option value.
Additional cost-free, ignorable policies cannot reduce optimal deterministic value.
Additional cost-free, ignorable policies cannot reduce expected value.
Additional cost-free, ignorable policies cannot reduce robust max-min value.
Net flexibility value can be negative.
Information
EVPI is nonnegative.
Free EVSI is nonnegative when the action set is unchanged.
EVSI cannot exceed EVPI.
More informative sigma algebras cannot reduce expected optimal value.
Information that never changes the optimal action has zero decision value.
Value of information is not value of computation.
Waiting
Waiting can have positive value.
Waiting can have negative value.
Time can destroy actions even while information improves.
Premature commitment can be arbitrarily worse than cost-free perfect-information adaptation.
Dynamic policies
Finite expected-utility commitment problems satisfy Bellman recursion under a sufficient state.
Physical geometry alone may be dynamically insufficient.
Commitment rights, contracts, and option status may be necessary Markov-state variables.
Robust strategy
Scenario-wise ideal plans do not form one nonanticipative strategy.
Rectangular ambiguity supports robust Bellman recursion.
Nonrectangular ambiguity can invalidate stagewise minimization.
Silent rectangularization can produce impossible worst-case combinations.
Static terminal CVaR need not be dynamically time consistent.
Commitment timing
Under bounded lead time, the latest robust commitment is (D-\overline L).
Option expiry can move the commitment date earlier.
Robust viability kernels characterize states with feasible robust continuation policies.
A commitment frontier is a state where waiting destroys robust viability.
At a frontier, a robustly feasible policy cannot wait.
Commitment closure bounds the value of pure additional information.
Just-in-time commitment
Later commitment is not automatically better.
Just-in-time commitment is defined only after higher-priority feasibility, sovereignty, and value obligations are satisfied.
Hardness
Minimum-cost preservation of a required future-option set is NP-hard.
Explicit scenario trees can grow exponentially.
Economic integration
A physically live option may be economically dead.
A supplier option may be probabilistic rather than guaranteed.
Procurement rights and reservation windows are part of option state.
Prompt-18 execution fibers remain authoritative for option exercise.
Sovereignty
Option value does not create architectural authority.
Human options and engineering options are distinct.
A valuable enabling change can still require consent.
Assurance
Commitment claims can be represented in a PCCP.
Incremental commitment recertification equals cold checking under complete dependencies.
PCCP semantics are independent of proposal source.
Explicit PCCP checking is linear in proof-DAG size plus local checker costs.
Whole-project staged commitment
A certified staged policy belongs to the current continuation fiber.
Certified robust policies are nonanticipative.
Live options retain their exact modality.
Reversibility certificates restore the declared contextual state.
EVPI, EVSI, and waiting claims remain model relative.
Viability and frontier claims provide certified timing boundaries.
Design freeze may reduce causal complexity only by removing future actions.
Prompt-11 assurance may consume only the commitment propositions the PCCP actually proves.



